  "Aqua Shard": "Aqua Shard drew 22,394 users in W25, 26% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 5.93% versus 5.91% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 1328 against 1796 a year ago. Google ran £1,968 for 345 bookings; Meta held 182 schedules at £15.61.",
  "Hutong": "Hutong drew 13,376 users in W25, 8% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 6.51% versus 6.86% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 871 against 994 a year ago. Google ran £1,481 for 201 bookings; Meta held 231 schedules at £9.44.",
  "Regent St": "Regent St drew 5,685 users in W25, 21% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 5.65% versus 4.09% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 321 against 293 a year ago. Google ran £783 for 64 bookings; Meta held 77 schedules at £13.56.",
  "Azzurra": "Azzurra drew 1,720 users in W25, 10% above the same FY week last year, with conversion at 5.23% versus 5.56% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 90 against 87 a year ago. Google ran £663 for 16 bookings; Meta held 54 schedules at £21.31.",
  "Shiro Sushi": "Shiro Sushi drew 1,236 users in W25, 37% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 9.47% versus 4.64% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 117 against 91 a year ago. Google ran £751 for 86 bookings; Meta held 40 schedules at £8.16.",
  "DSL": "DSL (Dim Sum Library) leads the portfolio on conversion at 10.74% on 5,315 users, with GA4 bookings of 571. NOTE: DSL rebranded, so the 2025 lines are pre-rebrand (Luci) and are NOT a like-for-like comparison — the apparent YoY gains are a rebrand artefact and last year's Google data does not exist on this account."
